-- title:
--   Inertia-invariant classes of J₁(Mp) extend over Pl after multiplication by n
-- statement:
--   The statement is formulated inside a long frame of data for $X_1(Mp)$ and its relative Picard scheme at a prime $p$; the hypotheses are grouped below, and every group is named.
--
--   *Arithmetic base.* A prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; a field $L$ of characteristic zero which is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, together with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity; an intermediate field $K$ of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with `hK` identifying $K$ with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ under coefficientwise extension of scalars; a discrete valuation domain $A$ with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ (`hAp`) and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$ (`hζA`), with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A \to L \to K$; and an element $j \in K$, nonzero, whose Laurent expansion is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant. The curve over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ is the two-chart model $\mathrm{modelTo} :=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252), the structure morphism to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ of the scheme glued from the spectra of the finite and infinite chart subalgebras of $K$ attached to $j$; it is assumed proper.
--
--   *Geometric special fibre.* An algebraically closed $A$-algebra field $k$ of characteristic $p$; two schemes $C_1, C_2$, proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral over $k$ via $c_1, c_2$; closed immersions $i_1, i_2$ of $C_1, C_2$ into the base change of $\mathrm{modelTo}$ along $A \to k$, commuting with the structure morphisms; the hypothesis `hcover` that every point of $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathrm{modelTo}, \mathrm{specMap}\,A\,k)$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$; `hred`, that the scheme-theoretic intersection $\mathrm{pullback}(i_1, i_2)$ is reduced; and a natural number $n > 0$ equal to the cardinality of that intersection (`hn`, `hn0`).
--
--   *Sections.* A section $\varepsilon$ of $\mathrm{modelTo}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, sections $\varepsilon_1, \varepsilon_2$ of $c_1, c_2$, and `hε₁`, asserting that $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ is the base-changed section `sectionBaseChange k ε`.
--
--   *Relative Picard data.* A designation $D$ (a scheme $D.P$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ with a zero section) together with `hrep`, the nonempty assertion that $D$ represents the subfunctor of the relative Picard functor of $\mathrm{modelTo}$ rigidified along $\varepsilon$ and cut out by `algEquivZeroCut`, i.e. by fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero: a Poincaré rigidified bundle satisfying that condition, the universal property that every such rigidified bundle on a base $T$ is induced by a unique morphism $T \to D.P$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, and triviality of the pullback along the zero section; moreover $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ is smooth (`hsm`) and separated (`hsep`). Over $k$: `hreps`, the corresponding representability statement for the base change of $\mathrm{modelTo}$ and of $D$ to $k$, and `hPk`, an isomorphism between its Poincaré bundle and the bundle obtained from the Poincaré bundle of $D$ by base change along $A \to k$. Designations $D_1, D_2$ over $k$ for $c_1, c_2$ with representability assertions `hrep₁`, `hrep₂`.
--
--   *Comparison with the component $C_2$.* A morphism $\nu_2$ from $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$ to $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,k$, subject to `hν₂`: for every $k$-scheme $t : T \to \mathrm{Spec}\,k$ and every $a$ over $t$ into $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle of $D_2$ along $a$ followed by $\nu_2$ is isomorphic to the rigidification along `rigSection c₂ t ε₂` of the pullback, along the curve-change morphism determined by $i_2$, of the pullback of the Poincaré bundle over $k$ along $a$.
--
--   *Generic fibre and its function field.* Algebra structures of $A$ and $L$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} = \mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\,\mathbb{Q}$ forming a scalar tower; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) (a proper smooth integral scheme with a ring isomorphism of that field with its function field and a bijection between closed points and places), an isomorphism $e_\eta$ from $M_\eta.C$ onto $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathrm{modelTo}, \mathrm{specMap}\,A\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ compatible with the structure morphisms (`heη`); the nonemptiness of the preimage under $e_\eta$ followed by the first projection of the finite chart open, and the pinning hypothesis `hMηpin`: for every element $a$ of the finite chart algebra [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.chartAlgFin A ↥K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L135), the element of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` obtained by transporting, through $M_\eta.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, the germ at the generic point of the pullback of $a$ has Laurent expansion the coefficientwise image along $L \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the Laurent expansion of $a$ in $K$.
--
--   *Galois equivariance.* `hgal`: for every $g \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ acting trivially on the image of $L$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, x'$ of $M_\eta.C$ such that $x'$ followed by $e_\eta$ and the first projection equals $\mathrm{Spec}(g)$ followed by the same composite for $x$, the place attached to $x'$ is the image of the place attached to $x$ under the action of [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)) g`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54).
--
--   *Special fibre group data.* A structure $G$ of type [`ModularCurve.JOneP.NeronSpecialFibreGeom p`](def/ModularCurve_JOnePGeom.html#L9), consisting of abelian groups $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$, a subgroup $G.\mathrm{torus}$ of $G.J0s$ and a surjective homomorphism $G.\mathrm{proj} : G.J0s \to G.JI \times G.JE$ with kernel $G.\mathrm{torus}$; bijections $\mathrm{pts}$, $\mathrm{pts}_I$, $\mathrm{pts}_E$ of $G.J0s$, $G.JI$, $G.JE$ with the $k$-sections of $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,k).\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_1.\mathrm{toBase}$, $D_2.\mathrm{toBase}$ respectively; additivity hypotheses `hadd`, `haddI`, `haddE`, stating in each case that the pullback of the relevant Poincaré bundle along the point attached to a sum is isomorphic to the tensor product of the pullbacks along the summands; and `hproj`, stating that $\mathrm{pts}_I$ of the first component of $G.\mathrm{proj}\,x$ is $\mathrm{pts}\,x$ followed by the morphism `RepresentsRelSubPic.pullbackHom` attached to $i_1$, and $\mathrm{pts}_E$ of the second component is $\mathrm{pts}\,x$ followed by $\nu_2$.
--
--   *Igusa identification of the components.* An integral weight-one form $w$ on $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $k$ (a weight-one modular form with an integral $q$-expansion whose reduction in $k$ is nonzero), and two curve models $\mathrm{Mdl}_1, \mathrm{Mdl}_2$ over $k$ of the Igusa function field [`ModularCurve.igusaFunctionFieldX1C k M w`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaFunctionFieldX1.html#L35), with isomorphisms $e_1 : \mathrm{Mdl}_1.C \cong C_1$ and $e_2 : \mathrm{Mdl}_2.C \cong C_2$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,k$ (`he₁`, `he₂`).
--
--   *The dictionary $\mathrm{gpts}$ and the Abel–Jacobi pinning.* A bijection $\mathrm{gpts}$ between [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the degree-zero divisor class group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$, additive for the relative group law induced by `hrep` (`hgadd`). Over $L$: the representability assertion `hDL` for the base change to $L$; a morphism $\mathrm{aj}_L$ from the base-changed curve to $(D.\mathrm{baseChange}\,L).\mathrm{toBase}$ over $L$ with `hajLε`, that the base-changed section composed with $\mathrm{aj}_L$ is the zero section, and `hajL`, the Abel–Jacobi property: for every field $K'$, every $t : \mathrm{Spec}\,K' \to \mathrm{Spec}\,L$ and every point $x$ of the base-changed curve over $t$, the pullback of the Poincaré bundle over $L$ along $x$ followed by $\mathrm{aj}_L$ is isomorphic to the line bundle of the relative effective Cartier divisor of the point $x$ tensored with the ideal module of the divisor of the section $t$ followed by the base-changed $\varepsilon$; a comparison morphism $k_L$ between the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$- and $L$-base changes compatible with both projections (`hkL₁`, `hkL₂`); a morphism $\overline{\mathrm{aj}} : M_\eta.C \to D.P$ defined by `hajbar` as $e_\eta$ followed by $k_L$, $\mathrm{aj}_L$ and the first projection, lying over $M_\eta.\mathrm{toBase}$ and $\mathrm{specMap}\,A\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (`hajbar_over`); an isomorphism `hPL` between the Poincaré bundle over $L$ and the one obtained by base change from $D$; a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\overline{\varepsilon}$ of $M_\eta.C$ lying over $\varepsilon$ (`hεbar`) and sent by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$ to the zero section (`hεbar_aj`); and `hpts_aj`, stating that for all $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $x, s$ of $M_\eta.C$ with $s$ lying over $\varepsilon$ there is a degree-zero divisor $D_v$ of `x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)` equal to the difference of the places of $x$ and of $s$, each with multiplicity one, whose class satisfies $\mathrm{gpts}(\,[D_v]\,) = x$ followed by $\overline{\mathrm{aj}}$.
--
--   *The place above $p$.* A valuation subring $\mathrm{Pl}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $\mathrm{Pl}$ (`hPl`), a ring homomorphism $\rho : A \to \mathrm{Pl}$ whose composite with the inclusion $\mathrm{Pl} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map of $A$ (`hρ`), and a surjective ring homomorphism $\pi_k : \mathrm{Pl} \to k$ with $\pi_k \circ \rho$ the structure map $A \to k$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every $x$ in [`ModularCurve.JOne (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), if $\sigma \bullet x = x$ holds for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ that lies in `Pl.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` (the image in the Galois group of the inertia subgroup of the decomposition subgroup of $\mathrm{Pl}$) and acts trivially on the image of $L$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, then there exists a morphism $z : \mathrm{Spec}\,\mathrm{Pl} \to D.P$ with $z$ followed by $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ equal to $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\rho$, such that the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point $\mathrm{gpts}(n \bullet x)$ of $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the inclusion $\mathrm{Pl} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ followed by $z$. Here $n$ is the number of points of the intersection $\mathrm{pullback}(i_1, i_2)$ of the two components of the geometric special fibre.
--
--   This is the component-group estimate at a place above $p$ for $J_1(Mp)$: the special fibre of the two-chart model over an unramified extension of $A$ has two components meeting in $n$ reduced points, so $n$ times an inertia-invariant class lies in the identity component and hence extends to a point of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ over the valuation ring $\mathrm{Pl}$. It feeds the bound on the cardinality of the inertia invariants of the torsion of $J_1(Mp)$ in terms of the number of points with values in the valuation subring.
